        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d6456b0f-bbc0-51e8-89eb-005f198cac7b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Leslie Skinner\n- Products: Bazooka, shoulder-fired missiles, rocket-propelled anti-tank weapons\n- Events: World War II\n\nFacts:\n- During World War II, Leslie Skinner played a leading role in developing several rocket-propelled weapons.\n- During World War II, Leslie Skinner notably helped develop the Bazooka as the first shoulder-fired missile system.\n- The Bazooka was also referred to as the \"Stovepipe.\"\n- The Bazooka was among the first generation of rocket-propelled anti-tank weapons used in infantry combat.\n- The Bazooka was an original type of shoulder-fired missile.\n- The name \"Bazooka\" is often used informally to refer to shoulder-fired missiles, although it does not technically define all such missiles.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "1e9b8288-d080-5e28-b5b9-4ee9ff38be8a",
        "text": "Page: Leslie Skinner. Sentence: He played a leading role in the development of several rocket propelled weapons during World War II, notably the first shoulder-fired missile system, the Bazooka.\nPage: Bazooka. Sentence: Also referred to as the \"Stovepipe\", the innovative bazooka was among the first generation of rocket-propelled anti-tank weapons used in infantry combat.\nPage: Shoulder-fired missile. Sentence: In many instances, although not technically defining all shoulder-fired missiles, the name Bazooka is used as an informal name regularly, although the actual Bazooka is a type of original shoulder-fired missile in its own right.",
